{
 "_name": "s29_mixed_leaf_team",
 "_desc": "P2-1 mixed-leaf team reachability (user-ratified 2026-07-20). ONE team whose members are homed onto DIFFERENT static layers that SHARE the PHY (freq/bw/sf) but differ in leaf NIBBLE: layer 20 (nibble 4) statics H20a(101)/H20b(102), layer 23 (nibble 7) static H23(111). Team members (real cleartext identities): T1 (0xEE000001, cfg layer 20) homes H20a; T2 (0xEE000002, cfg layer 23) homes H23; T3 (0xEE000003, cfg layer 22 = a THIRD nibble 6) stays OFF-GRID (no static on nibble 6 in range) + team-DADs. All three mutually in range. Pre-2026-07-20 the beacon + team-scoped-H leaf gates dropped a foreign-nibble team frame BEFORE the team check, so a mixed-leaf team could never FORM (_rt_team) or RESOLVE (team H) across nibbles — the F/RTS carve-outs were dead scope. This scenario proves the fix: (1) cross-nibble _rt_team forms + a team DM by hash T1->T2 delivers (leaf-4 <-> leaf-7); (2) a team DM by hash T3->T1 delivers (off-grid nibble-6 -> homed nibble-4, cross-nibble team hash resolves); (3) a team CHANNEL post reaches ALL members across all three nibbles (RTS-M + DATA-M leaf-exempt for a team flood); (4) CONTAINMENT: the statics NEVER id_bind a team member's key (team beacons stay off the static hash-locate plane). The team-PHY home-refusal (Level 2) is proven by the native unit tests (the sim harness cannot drive the direct-adopt `mobile register` console path, and an off-grid member never pulls a layer directory so cannot learn a foreign-PHY layer in-sim). Cleartext (no seeds) — encrypted team DMs are s22-covered. Deterministic; run 3x. QA-review into simulation/ + anchor.",
